// The Kitchen Garden's tilemap, 340 × 150 — from
// design_handoff_level_04_kitchen_garden_v2. Today's garden is at (0, 0),
// rows 0-71, cols 0-169, tile for tile, but for its three new ways down: the
// sinkhole in the orchard (cols 84-88) to the Mole Warren, the trapdoor in
// the root cellar's floor (col 141) to the Ice House, and the ladder down the
// outside of the east wall (col 170). Past them, east over the wall and down
// under it all:
//
//   D · the Vineyard Terraces (cols 170-235, rows 11-80): the noria out of
//     the millpond, the pergola, the windpump, the wine cellar;
//   E · the Orangery and its boiler room (cols 236-300, rows 1-72);
//   F · the Yew Maze and the Badger Sett (cols 298-339, rows 26-100);
//   G · the Pump House, the Mushroom Caves and the Irrigation Channel (cols
//     168-339, rows 73-114);
//   C · the Ice House (cols 106-168, rows 72-114);
//   A · the Mole Warren, B · the Culvert and the Frog Grotto (cols 0-108,
//     rows 72-118);
//   J · the Old Aqueduct (cols 8-335, rows 116-148), either side of the
//     Spring chamber.
//
// The handoff's rows had not been played (its README says so), and
// kitchen-garden.test.ts walked them to find where they broke. They differ
// from the handoff where it did, and only there:
//   - the sinkhole cut the garden's walk five tiles wide: its west lip is a
//     tile back (col 84), a jump from the low branch of apple tree B;
//   - the Frozen Swan's ledge runs on to col 117, a jump off an ice block at
//     tier 94's west end;
//   - in the orangery, four staging platforms are a column nearer the one
//     before (rows 44, 49, 46 and 40), and a step at the foot of the vent
//     (267, 54) is the way onto the staging east over the cactus bed while
//     the vent is still off;
//   - the boiler room's platforms are three rows over its floor (row 68), a
//     catwalk crosses the hot pipes, its first shaft is three tiles across,
//     and a ladder runs down it (col 290) to the coal store — the way to the
//     vent lever and the sluice lever that does not need the vent;
//   - the culvert's water stands at row 108, under its posts and walkway, not
//     three rows below them, and its posts are a jump apart and from the
//     tube down to the aqueduct (cols 47-49, 57-59);
//   - the frog grotto's outer lily pads are a column nearer the middle one,
//     and a ledge (row 101, cols 91-92) is the step up to Old Toad's Stone;
//   - the Ice House's pool stands a row higher (from row 105), a step under
//     its floors, and its east wall meets the channel's water;
//   - the channel's brick posts stand a row over its water and stop two rows
//     short of its bed: one long swim, as the handoff means it to be;
//   - the gear room has a ladder (col 176) from the Ice-cutters' passage to
//     its floor, and the inspection tube's ladder (col 184) reaches down to
//     the Spring pool;
//   - the Spring pool's banks are a step over its water, its sides are earth,
//     and the troughs end in brick where they reach the chamber;
//   - every aqueduct pier stops three rows over the walk — arches, which the
//     walk goes under — and each sump's timber step is under its hole;
//   - the ladder up to the sett (col 320) reaches down to the trough;
//   - the estate well has ladders: from the ground to the well chamber
//     (col 335), and on down to the channel's water (col 330);
//   - in the wine cellar, the east vat is as tall as the Great Vat beside it;
//   - in the yew maze, four walls have a gap (cols 312-319) so that every
//     floor's hole up can be reached;
//   - the sett's and the Root Chamber's thorny roots are two tiles across,
//     not three, which no jump clears.
//
// Legend (see CHAR_TO_TILE in tilemap.ts):
//   . sky   a autumn turf   D soil   B CastleBrick   F CastleFloor (flags)
//   T timber   H ladder   W water   U puffball   V vine   X bramble (a
//   cactus, hot pipes or thorny roots, by where it is)   ^ updraft (pulsed)
//   Q yew hedge   Y the sluice gate (a Portcullis entity)
